+# Secrets used by config/deploy.yml. Fill these in before running
+# `bin/kamal setup`.
+#
+# You can either:
+#
+#   1. Export the variables in your shell (or load them from your password
+#      manager) before running Kamal, leaving the references below untouched.
+#   2. Or replace each `$VARIABLE` reference below with the secret value
+#      itself. If you do that, keep the values out of git — this file is
+#      tracked. `git update-index --skip-worktree .kamal/secrets` will make
+#      git ignore your local changes to it. Quote values that contain special
+#      characters (e.g. `SMTP_PASSWORD='pa$$word'`).
+#
+# Generate a SECRET_KEY_BASE with:
+#   bin/rails secret
+#
+# Generate VAPID keys (used for browser push notifications) with:
+#   bundle exec ruby -rweb-push -e 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+
+SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
+SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
+VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+
+# If you switch from the local registry to Docker Hub, GHCR, etc., you'll also
+# need a registry password for the registry configured in config/deploy.yml:
+# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
